A||N||8||Monkeyman||Dash Connections||||1||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||08-31-2000||01:37 PM||||I just pulled the dash from the Grape Ape in preparation for the new one (still need to make a mock up).  I noticed that there is a plastic electrical connection box in the left hand corner just under the windshield.  It looks like the wires for the courtesy lights plug in there but I'm not sure.  What is this for & can it be easily moved?  I'd like as much of my wiring to be centrally located as possible.  Also, how difficult would it be to move the location of my fuse box?  It hangs down just above the drivers side dead pedal.  Kind of in the way and it'll be visible once the new dash is in place. <P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||08-31-2000||01:49 PM||||Monkey,<P>The wiring harness and their switches/connectors can be moved around  anywhere you want, including the fuse box. Everything just lays in under the dash and is held up with plastic clips. Be forwarned... If you move too much at one time it'll be like trying to untangle cold spaghetti. Be careful and lable each connector as you remove or move them.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||08-31-2000||02:05 PM||||I still need to know what this connection box is for, but at least I know that I can move things.  Glad to hear it.  It'll make my job a little easier.  (BTW--I happen to like cold spaghetti! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||08-31-2000||02:09 PM||||The shop manual calls it an "accessory junction box".  It's clipped into some holes in the side of the chassis.  On mine the power windows and the interior lights get their power feeds from that box.  I think power mirrors and door locks would also plug in there.  Have fun with the wire moving!!  ||||reg||7
Z||000004||theogre||08-31-2000||02:33 PM||||I had my dash out to install the power windows harness..... I'd leave that wiring where it is. There are some rather high current lines in there if you have power windows. You don't want to splice such things needlessly.<P>In the life of the car the only reason anyone would mess with that terminal box is to add an assesory like power windows to a car that doesn't have them. Or some similar thing as that. There's almost no reason to ever mess with it otherwise.<P>Altho if you aren't going to have speaker holes in about the stock locations I'd lower it down on the post so it can be reached.<P>Cortesy lights connect there, including the low mount ones in the foot wells. Power windows connect to a terminal there. (This box is already wired to the fuse box even if the power windows aren't installed. All you need is the circuit breaker and the terminal is ready to use.) A couple other things go there but I can't remember what.<P>The fuse box itself is on a plastic bracket that also holds the low mount courtesy light. You can alter/move the thing but be carefull. there's not allot of slack in the harness. make sure you don't have it up against anything sharp.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-31-2000||02:35 PM||||I don't plan on moving anything I don't have to (like the fuse box).  I just want to know that I can if I need to.<P>Thanx a ton, guys!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||08-31-2000||02:38 PM||||The speaker holes will be in the same locations but much smaller.  I think I'll move that down a little farther just in case.  The Grape Ape is already fully optioned, but I hate taking chances.  Other than moving it, I'll leave it alone.  I will have to move the fuse box, though.  Probably just a little higher (up out of the way) so it's not seen.  Hopefully I won't have to mess with any of the wires that way.  I'll have to mess with the wires, though, to install new switches (once I find some that will work).||||reg||1
Z||000007||HugGRRRFiero||08-31-2000||02:46 PM||||Yep, that's a junction box.  The legs of the box are clips that hold it to the body.  You can remove the whole box from the side without unplugging anything so you can mark everything and then clip it back.  It's very important mark everything with tape, for example A to A, B to B.  It takes a little bit of time, but in the end it will save a lot of guess work.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||08-31-2000||11:52 PM||||I plan on marking and remarking (and then maybe remarking again) every single wire.  I don't want to take any chances.  I want this done right.  If I can't do it right, I'll put the original interior back in, drink a beer or two and scream really loud.  I'll make a mock up as soon as I can get some big enough cardboard.<P>Who was it that offered their help if I emailed a sketch??  Email me again.  I accidentally deleted most of my emails.||||reg||1
